st-Georgia Tech game speaks on 'Today' show","description":"The couple's intense discussion was caught on an ESPN broadcast of Wake Forest and Georgia Tech's Week 12 game and went viral.","published":"2026-11-24T21:02:51.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584732/wake-forest-georgia-tech-viral-couple-speaks","type":"Story","byline":"Kalan Hooks","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Colorado's Deion Sanders shrugs off hot-seat chatter before UCF","description":"Deion Sanders handles outside chatter -- in this case, speculation over his future as coach at Colorado -- by simply tuning out the noise.","published":"2026-11-24T21:29:37.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585728/colorado-sanders-shrugs-hot-seat-chatter-ucf","type":"HeadlineNews","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Memphis' Charles Huff says he's not candidate for Maryland head coaching job","description":"Memphis' Charles Huff said he's not a candidate for the head coaching vacancy at Maryland and will not be part of this year's coaching carousel.","published":"2026-11-24T20:33:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585465/charles-huff-says-not-candidate-maryland-hc-job","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Adam Rittenberg","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"NCAA sanctions Liberty over tampering with two players before entering portal","description":"Among the penalties the NCAA announced against Liberty, two coaches and the GM received show-cause penalties over tampering.","published":"2026-11-24T20:05:21.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50585093/ncaa-sanctions-liberty-transfer-portal-tampering","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Max Olson","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Five-star OT Lincoln Fa'alafi commits to Notre Dame, to join 2028 class","description":"New Zealand native Lincoln Fa'alafi, ESPN's No. 8 overall prospect in the 2028 cycle, committed Tuesday to Notre Dame.","published":"2026-11-24T19:56:07.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50584881/notre-dame-gets-2028-commitment-ot-lincoln-faalafi","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Eli Lederman","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"A timeline of Michigan athletics since 2017","description":"Warde Manuel's eventful decade in Ann Arbor has been marked by athletic successes and marred by controversy.","published":"2026-11-24T18:47:39.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/49351177/2026-michigan-warde-manuel-athletic-department-tenure-line-investigation","type":"Story","byline":"Paolo Uggetti","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"What are the conference title game clinching scenarios in Week 13?","description":"Plenty of spots are still up for grabs entering the final week of the regular season.","published":"2026-11-24T18:22:10.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583399/conference-title-game-clinching-scenarios-week-13","type":"Story","byline":"ESPN","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Trev Alberts told he won't be Michigan AD after agreement","description":"Trev Alberts was \"shocked and disheartened\" to be informed by the search firm representing Michigan that he will not be the Wolverines' next AD, he told ESPN.","published":"2026-11-25T00:44:32.000+00:00","url":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/story/_/id/50583155/attorney-trev-alberts-told-next-ad-michigan","type":"HeadlineNews","byline":"Pete Thamel and Dan Wetzel","source":"ESPN"}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/college-football/player/_/id/5031157/reed-harris","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)"},"pick":{"pick":50,"round":2,"team":"SEA","provisional":false},"wiki":{"rules":4,"title":"Reed Harris (American football)","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reed_Harris_(American_football)","description":"American football player","touched":"2026-11-22T04:18:14Z","intro":"Reed Harris is an American football wide receiver for the Arizona State Sun Devils. He previously played for the Boston College Eagles.","sections":[{"key":"early","title":"Early life","text":"Harris was born in Minnesota, and moved to Conrad, Montana when he was a year old, growing up on a 12,000 acre farm. Harris moved to Great Falls, Montana when he was in 8th grade, later attending Great Falls High School where he was the football team's starting quarterback as a sophomore and junior. He moved to wide receiver during his senior season and finished with 553 yards and three touchdowns. Harris finished his high school career completing 229 passes for 21 touchdowns, while adding 1,575 yards and 13 touchdowns on the ground, with 36 receptions for 536 yards and four touchdowns through the air. He also added 83 tackles with ten being for a loss, nine sacks, five fumble recoveries, and a forced fumble on defense. Coming out of high school, Harris was rated as a three-star recruit in football, basketball, and track by 247Sports, and was ranked as the top player in the state of Montana in the class of 2023. He committed to play college football for the Boston College Eagles over offers from other schools such as Iowa State, Oregon State, Montana, Montana State, Colorado State, Utah State, San Diego State, Central Michigan, Harvard, Idaho, and Idaho State."},{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"BOSTON COLLEGE\nAs a freshman in 2023, Harris appeared in four games, making one catch, as he was redshirted. In week 2 of the 2024 season, he caught his first career touchdown in a win over Duquesne. During the 2024 season, Harris played in all 13 games with 11 starts, catching 17 passes for 486 yards and four touchdowns. During the 2025 season, he totaled 39 catches for 673 yards and five touchdowns; after the conclusion of the season, he entered the NCAA transfer portal."}]}}